  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 2.3. Increased capacity of the ILO constituents to engage in a forward-looking international labour standards policy</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">A Tripartite Committee was set up in early 2021 to oversee the implementation of the DWCP for Iraq. The ILO facilitated dialogue between the tripartite constituents besides encouraging and proposing the establishment of a tripartite mechanism to oversee the implementation of the DWCP.</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">2.3.2 Number of member States with tripartite mechanisms enabling constituents to effectively engage in the implementation of international labour standards at the national level, including reporting to the supervisory bodies</narrative>
    </title>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 2.1. Increased capacity of the member States to ratify international labour standards</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Iraq ratified  the Safety and Health in Agriculture Convention, 2001 (No. 184) on 21 May 2021 and the Seafarers&apos; Identity Documents Convention (Revised), 2003, as amended (No. 185) on 21 May 2021. Advice and technical assistance were provided on  labour-related legislation with a view to strengthening the legal and institutional national framework and building a more conducive environment for decent work. Reviews of draft legislation and technical assistance aimed at improving national frameworks was provided on C184 by both the DWT and TC Project focusing on decent work in agriculture. Support included technical advice on the contents of OSH-related Conventions and assistance for the development of a national OSH profile, policy and programme in consultation with the social partners and capacity building on OSH. Support was also provided to develop a national system for the notification, recording and investigation of occupational accidents, injuries and diseases and to strengthen the capacity of the social partners and tripartite structures and mechanisms for OSH promotion and labour inspection, including in the agriculture sector.</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">2.1.2. Number of ratifications of up-to-date technical Conventions, including those recommended by the Governing Body in the context of the Standards Review Mechanism</narrative>
    </title>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 2.3. Increased capacity of the ILO constituents to engage in a forward-looking international labour standards policy</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Office received all article 22 reports within the deadline, including an early detailed report in response to a CAS case concerning application of C111. Technical assistance was provided to the MOLSA and the social partners, including through a face-to-face 2-day training on Reporting on Ratified and Unratified ILO Conventions in August 2021. Follow up support and policy advice on steps to be taken to address CAS Conclusions was also provided during face-to-face meetings and virtual follow up support.</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">2.3.1. Percentage of reports on the application of ratified Conventions due by 1 September received in a timely manner that include replies to comments of the supervisory bodies</narrative>
    </title>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
